From: Il tuo nome <tu@esempio.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:55:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell/native_raminit: Log GEN_PMCON_2 with the
 boot mode

The boot mode of the native RAM init comes from DISB and MEM_SR in
GEN_PMCON_2: both set make a warm boot, which keeps the memory and takes
the fast path. A reset that romstage does before raminit for an option
(Hyper-Threading, the Ethernet switch, VT-x) could look like a warm
reset during training, which discards the training data.

Log the register, so that the case can be told from the log. On a
ThinkPad W541 it does not arise: at the boot after such a reset DISB or
MEM_SR is clear (0x2024 and 0x2080 at two cold boots with the
Hyper-Threading reset), so the RAM init takes the boot as a cold one
and uses its cache.

TEST=On a ThinkPad W541 with the native RAM init, the Hyper-Threading
option off and on: GEN_PMCON_2 logged at every boot, the cache used at
all 8 boots of the test.

Change-Id: I0790abb7032fe051440a3967dc68b590acd23d8e
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
index 06aef201af..9d38c42bb4 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.c
@@ -37,6 +37,10 @@ static enum raminit_boot_mode get_boot_mode(void)
 {
 	const uint16_t pmcon_2 = pci_read_config16(PCH_LPC_DEV, GEN_PMCON_2);
 	const uint16_t bitmask = GEN_PMCON_2_DISB | GEN_PMCON_2_MEM_SR;
+
+	/* DISB and MEM_SR together make a warm boot, which may keep the memory */
+	printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "GEN_PMCON_2: 0x%04x\n", pmcon_2);
+
 	return (pmcon_2 & bitmask) == bitmask ? BOOTMODE_WARM : BOOTMODE_COLD;
 }
 
